WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.680
In the United States of America, an historically
bizarre series of events has been unfolding.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:09.540
When the sitting president, Donald Trump,
helped to foment public outrage with false

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:14.580
claims of election tampering, it led to a
violent insurrection by right-wing protesters

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:19.670
who descended on the U.S. Capitol, resulting
in destruction, theft, and multiple deaths.

00:00:19.670 --> 00:00:23.100
Those events took place on January 6, 2021.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.689
Two days later, Twitter made the decision
to permanently ban Trump from the social media

00:00:27.689 --> 00:00:29.570
platform, with @TwitterSafety writing:

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:34.630
"...we have permanently suspended the account
due to the risk of further incitement of violence."

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:39.770
While people online debated the benefits and
drawbacks of that decision, the House of Representatives

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:43.630
immediately set to work on drafting up Articles
of Impeachment.

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:49.100
And on January 13, 2021, Trump became the
only president in United States history to

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:50.630
be impeached twice.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:54.680
In the midst of all of that, a question arose:
If we can hypothetically remove Trump from

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:58.990
office mere days before he would be leaving
anyway, what else can he be removed from?

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:03.070
The answer, as usual, comes from Twitter,
where someone had the bright idea to propose

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:06.720
removing Trump's brief cameo in Home Alone
2: Lost in New York.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:07.720
Priorities, right?

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.050
"Excuse me, where's the lobby?

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.610
Down the hall and to the left."

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:15.313
The idea went one step further than just removing
Trump from the movie.

00:01:15.313 --> 00:01:19.610
Instead of just deleting the scene, one Twitter
user made the case for giving young Kevin

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:21.870
an eerie vision of the future, calling for:

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:27.320
"[A] petition to digitally replace Trump in
Home Alone 2 with 40-year-old Macaulay Culkin.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.320
"

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.340
Macaulay Culkin, star of the first two Home
Alone films, is very internet savvy.

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:35.680
He's collaborated with multiple people in
recent years to create comedic content -- much

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:38.170
of which pokes fun at his most famous role.

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:42.464
It's safe to say that the former Kevin McCallister
still has a lot of fun with Home Alone hot takes.

00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:46.750
Naturally, that means people can't feel truly
assured that Donald Trump should be removed

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:50.150
from Home Alone 2 until the star himself gives
his blessing.

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:52.620
And guess who showed up to do just that?

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:55.180
"Can I help you?"

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:56.460
"It's me.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:57.740
It's Macaulay."

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:02.409
After much discussion, Culkin weighed in on
the original tweet, responding with one simple

00:02:02.409 --> 00:02:03.409
word: "Sold."

00:02:03.409 --> 00:02:07.460
But how did that surprise cameo in Home Alone
2 even happen in the first place?

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:11.110
It probably won't come as a surprise to hear
that Donald Trump was more responsible than

00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:13.800
anyone else for his brief cameo in Home Alone
2.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:18.790
In an interview with Insider, Home Alone director
Chris Columbus revealed the entire oddball

00:02:18.790 --> 00:02:21.900
story behind Trump's brief moment in the film,
saying:

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:26.150
"Like most locations in New York City, you
just pay a fee and you are allowed to shoot

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:27.280
in that location.

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:31.967
We approached The Plaza Hotel, which Trump
owned at the time, because we wanted to shoot in the lobby.

00:02:31.967 --> 00:02:34.390
We couldn't rebuild The Plaza on a soundstage.

00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:35.390
Trump said okay."

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:39.720
However, in what also won't come as a surprise
to many, Trump's go-ahead came with a somewhat

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.060
self-centered catch.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.210
Columbus went on to say:

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:46.899
"We paid the fee, but he also said, 'The only
way you can use the Plaza is if I'm in the movie.

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:50.709
So we agreed to put him in the movie, and
when we screened it for the first time the

00:02:50.709 --> 00:02:54.200
oddest thing happened: people cheered when
Trump showed up on-screen.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.300
So I said to my editor, 'Leave him in the
movie.

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:58.069
It's a moment for the audience.'

00:02:58.069 --> 00:03:00.060
But he did bully his way into the movie."

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:04.840
So, what are the chances that Disney actually
would digitally remove Trump and replace him

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:06.250
with an older Macaulay Culkin?

00:03:06.250 --> 00:03:11.307
The Home Alone franchise is a Fox property,
which means it's also, now, a Disney property.

00:03:11.307 --> 00:03:15.520
And if there's one thing we know about Disney+
, it's that the people behind the platform

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:18.138
don't mind editing old movies to include weird
stuff.

00:03:18.138 --> 00:03:19.648
"Maclunkey."

00:03:20.969 --> 00:03:25.230
The classic Tom Hanks mermaid comedy Splash,
for example, has a scene where Darryl Hannah's

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:29.620
butt has been digitally hidden by CGI hair,
as she runs towards the ocean.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:32.610
Suffice to say, there was no such CGI in the
original film.

00:03:32.610 --> 00:03:34.760
As for a Macaulay swap in Home Alone 2?

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:38.920
Well, the chances aren't great, but it's certainly
worth noting that Trump's cameo was already

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:44.930
cut from Canadian broadcast network CBC's
airing of Home Alone 2 as far back as 2014,

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:46.030
according to The Guardian.

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:47.030
Who knows?

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:51.190
Maybe next year we'll be watching this Christmas
classic on Disney+ with a few seconds missing.

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:53.840
"Merry Christmas, ya filthy animal."

